Brief Explanation:
This approach moves all non‑zero elements to the front of the array while maintaining their relative order. It keeps a pointer (pos) to track where the next non‑zero number should be placed. After processing all elements, the remaining positions are filled with zeros.
Time Complexity:

O(n) — The array is traversed once.

Space Complexity:

O(1) — The operation is done in place without extra space.

